- `internal/db/released_test.go`: `TestReleasedQueriesParse` runs every query in every `internal/db/testdata/released/<version>.json` through `db.Parse`, the same check `/api/q` makes. Each file maps a query name (section first, e.g. `who.people`) to its text. A failure names the version, the query and the reason. The test fails outright if it finds no files. Policy definitions (`sidebar_group`, `manages`) come from the server's compiled policy source, so a released query that calls one also guards that definition.
